Timing clearly way off but was this take essentially right? Not a victory lap by any means since $GOOGL went on to go a lot higher right after and I wasn’t/wouldn’t short Google. 

Nevertheless this seems to be exactly what it’s being punished for? That AI has eroded the old cash cow search without pointing out a clear path to a new one? 

@lipko has a good post on how the falling revenue per search in AI mode reflects partly an active effort from Google to optimize for better click-through rates and more relevant ads, so advertisers can end up paying more per click while getting higher-quality traffic that converts better. Remains to be seen if this works and persuades advertisers.

